assed, or Shifted in Locus?</article-title><source>J Exp Psychol Hum Percept Perform</source><year>2005</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>122</fpage><lpage>144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15709868</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0096-1523.31.1.122</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sladden</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How do general practitioners manage rectal bleeding?</article-title><source>Aust Fam Physician</source><year>1998</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>78</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9503712</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rankin</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hughes-Anderson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>House</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Heath</surname><given-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Aitken</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>House</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Costs of accessing surgical specialists by rural and remote residents</article-title><source>Aust N Z J Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>544</fpage><lpage>547</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1440-1622.2001.02188.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jong</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Vale</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Armstrong</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rural inequalities in cancer care and outcome</article-title><source>Med J Aust</source><year>2005</year><vo